spoint deployed singleplayer regression 'sillos appears late / player never appears': LoadingMachine.js soft fallback (after: LOADING_FALLBACK_MS 10s -> ready) fired UNCONDITIONALLY, lifting the loading screen before the gh-pages cold-booting BrowserServer Web Worker connected. Witnessed deployed connected:false at 25s then connected:true playerId:1 statePlayers:1 by ~40s (browser-413/414/416); local worker boots fast so it never reproduced locally. The worker module-graph fetch on a static host takes well over 10s. FIX (commit 13a447e3): gate the soft fallback on hasContent=(firstSnapshot && environment) on BOTH loading+checking states, plus an unconditional LOADING_HARD_MS 45s ceiling so a worker that genuinely never connects still surfaces the page. Happy path: ready still reached the instant content arrives (browser-417). loading-machine.test.js fallback test now waits the 45s hard stop. Lesson: any unconditional loading-curtain timeout races a legitimately-slow async boot; gate the lift on real scene content, keep only an absolute hard-stop unconditional.